+// EDEN_NX2_ACQUIRE_NODRAIN=1: semaphore acquires no longer drain the back before reading the
+// word. The back's releases still reach the waiter: a release it runs latches the pending
+// acquire (Nx2SemaphoreWaiters::OnWrite), and a word the GPU wrote into the buffer cache is
+// still flushed first (ReadSemaphoreWord). Ocarina of Time keeps a channel suspended on a
+// CPU-released semaphore most of the frame, and the front polled it every 50 us with a full
+// drain each time: the front could never run ahead of the back, so the split gained ~2%
+// there (12.7 vs 13.0 fps with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=0) against +54% elsewhere.
+bool AcquireNoDrain() {
+    static const bool value = [] {
+        const char* text = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_ACQUIRE_NODRAIN");
+        return text != nullptr && text[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return value;
+}
